OTOGAKURE — VILLAGE POLICY
CURSED SEAL ASSIGNMENT
Issued under the authority of Lord Orochimaru

Purpose
To govern who is offered the Cursed Seal, under what conditions, and to what end. The seal
is a limited investment of Lord Orochimaru's own chakra and is not bestowed lightly.

Eligibility
1. Only operatives whose chakra reserve meets the standing threshold may be considered.
2. Candidates must demonstrate loyalty beyond question. The seal ties a bearer to Lord
   Orochimaru's will; it is not to be placed on the unproven.
3. Assignment requires the sponsorship of an officer and the countersignature of the Head
   Medic.

Conditions
- Every candidate signs the application form acknowledging the risk of death.
- Application is performed only in the medic wing (Zone B) with a medic present.
- Survivors are entered to the seal-bearer registry and the health-monitoring schedule.

Use
- Level 1 use is at the bearer's discretion in the field, within monitoring limits.
- Level 2 use requires prior authorization and is barred to bearers graded unstable.

Failure and Refusal
Non-survivors are logged and disposed per compound protocol. A candidate who refuses the
seal after selection is reassessed for continued usefulness to the village.
